{"id":222,"name":"corsola","speciesId":222,"dex":222,"form":"normal","generation":2,"types":["water","rock"],"stats":{"hp":65,"attack":55,"defense":95,"special-attack":65,"special-defense":95,"speed":35},"abilities":[{"name":"hustle","hidden":false},{"name":"natural-cure","hidden":false},{"name":"regenerator","hidden":true}],"height":6,"weight":50,"baseExp":144,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/222.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/222.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/222.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/222.ogg","genus":"Coral Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon Coral","flavor":[{"version":"gold","text":"It continuously sheds and grows. The tip of its head is prized as a treasure for its beauty."},{"version":"silver","text":"In a south sea nation, the people live in communi­ ties that are built on groups of these POKéMON."},{"version":"crystal","text":"The points on its head absorb nutrients from clean water. They cannot survive in polluted water."},{"version":"ruby","text":"CORSOLA’s branches glitter very beautifully in seven colors when they catch sunlight. If any branch breaks off, this POKéMON grows it back in just one night."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"Clusters of CORSOLA congregate in warm seas where they serve as ideal hiding places for smaller POKéMON. When the water temperature falls, this POKéMON migrates to the southern seas."},{"version":"emerald","text":"CORSOLA live in warm southern seas. If the sea becomes polluted, the beautiful coral stalks become discolored and crumble away in tatters."},{"version":"firered","text":"In a south sea nation, the people live in communities that are built on groups of these POKéMON."},{"version":"diamond","text":"Many live in the clean seas of the south. They apparently can’t live in polluted waters."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"It continuously sheds and grows. The tip of its head is prized as a treasure because of its beauty."},{"version":"soulsilver","text":"In a south-sea nation, the people live in communities that are built on groups of these Pokémon."},{"version":"black-2","text":"They prefer unpolluted southern seas. Their coral branches lose their color and deteriorate in dirty water."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Corsola’s branches glitter very beautifully in seven colors when they catch sunlight. If any branch breaks off, this Pokémon grows it back in just one night."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Clusters of Corsola congregate in warm seas where they serve as ideal hiding places for smaller Pokémon. When the water temperature falls, this Pokémon migrates to the southern seas."},{"version":"sun","text":"Coral branches grow from its head. They break off quite easily, but they grow back in about three days."},{"version":"moon","text":"Pursued by Mareanie for the branches on its head, this Pokémon will sometimes snap its own branches off as a diversion while it escapes."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"The pink of Corsola that live in Alola is deep and vibrant, thanks to seas filled with nutrition."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"In Alola, where their natural enemies Mareanie are plentiful, many Corsola have stubby branches on their heads."},{"version":"sword","text":"It will regrow any branches that break off its head. People keep particularly beautiful Corsola branches as charms to promote safe childbirth."},{"version":"shield","text":"These Pokémon live in warm seas. In prehistoric times, many lived in the oceans around the Galar region as well."}],"flavorPt":"Esses Pokémon vivem em mares quentes. Em tempos pré-históricos, muitos também viviam nos oceanos ao redor da região de Galar.","genderRate":6,"captureRate":60,"eggGroups":["water1","water3"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evol